// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
// Filename:	ML PRO 2 Control PCB.test
// Project:		ML PRO 2 
// Author:      Foster & Freeman Ltd - Paul Evans
// Modified:    09.08.2024 Rev2 
// 
// Description: Tests the 12V, 3.3V, I2C, EEPROM, USB, FTDI, motor and hall sensors connections
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.
#1: Enter operator initials and PCB serial number:
a. Enter operator intials.
b. Enter serial number into the box above.
COMMENT: *Example image below*
IMPORTANT: Observe ESD precautions for handling ESD sensitive devices.  
DISPLAY: ControlSetup.jpg
CLICK_OK:

#2: Setup equipment 1
a. Set the adjustable PSU output(1) to 12V ±0.1V, 1.5A ±0.1A and switch the output to off.
b. Set the adjustable PSU output(2) to 5V ±0.1V , 0.2 A ±0.1A and switch the output to off.
c. Using TE060, connect the PSU output(1) to FT1 & FT2 on the Control PCB. 
d. Using TE195, connect the PSU output(2) to X10 on the Control PCB.
COMMENT: *Example image below*
DISPLAY: ControlSetup.jpg
CLICK_OK:

#2.1: Setup equipment 2
a. Connect the TE001 I/O Power button to J4 on the Control PCB.
b. Connect the PC (via Micro USB3 ) to the ML PRO 2 Control PCB (SK5 ).
c. On the PSU press the Output button for both PSU outputs.
d. Press the I/O Power button (TE001) to turn on the Control PCB.
DISPLAY: ControlSetup.jpg
COMMENT: *Example image below*
CLICK_OK:

#3: Connecting to the PSU
CONNECT: TENMAPSU
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #3: 

#4: Configure the PSU
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCP1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET1:500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:12.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:1.500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET2:12.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET2:1.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH2:1

#4.1: Power on the test box.
a. Press the I/O Power button to turn on the UUT.
DELAY: 9000
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.085 0.015 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
IF:
GOTO: #4.2: 
IMPORTANT: This test has failed, check the power button has been pressed, power supply, USB connection and the ftdi chip.		
PASS_FAIL: #4.1:
GOTO: #5

#4.2: Connect to test box
CONNECT: MLPRO2
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #2:

#5: PCB Program version check
COMMAND: MLPRO2 BUILD // will need to be updated when Fw is released
READLINE: MLPRO2 BUILD
IF:
Check the Returned result is current version as per TD037 PCB Programming Data Register.
COMMAND: MLPRO2 TYPE
READLINE: MLPRO2 TYPE
Returned product is = %TYPE%
Returned Version is = %BUILD%
ELSE:
Bad result . . . no communication
PASS_FAIL: #5


#6: Voltage check
COMMAND: MLPRO2 ReadVolts
READLINE: MLPRO2 ReadVolts
Returned Voltage is = %ReadVolts%
RANGE: %ReadVolts% 12000 15					
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#7: Tests the I2C to the EEPROM and 3.3V supply
COMMAND: MLPRO2 ENUM
READLINE: MLPRO2 ENUM
Check the expected result is a match.
Expected result is = EEPROM,
Returned result is = %ENUM%
[%ENUM% STR_EQ EEPROM,] // evaluates inside the [] and set true or false flag
SUB: TestPassOrFail // sends the outcome to flag to the subroutine for evaluation


#8: USB3 and USB2 ports test
a. Test K6 using the USB tester (TE013) and check that USB3 enumerated is displayed.
b. Test K3 using the USB tester (TE013) and check that USB3 enumerated is displayed.
c. Test both ports on CONN7 using the USB tester (TE013) and check that USB2 enumerated is displayed. 
d. Test both ports on CONN6 using the USB tester (TE013) and check that USB2 enumerated is displayed. 
PASS_FAIL: #8


#9: Test filter wheel driver and hall sensor feedback.
a. Connect the Motor Driver and Hall Sensor Jig (TE212) to the CONN2 and J3 on the UUT.
b. Click OK to continue.
IMPORTANT: Ensure that the Brown cable is fitted in the correct orientation.
DISPLAY: Filterwheel.png
CLICK_OK:
COMMAND: MLPRO2 C1h // home it
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: MLPRO2 C1X // read the vaule to check if the hall sensor is activated 
READLINE: MLPRO2 FILTER_Hall 
Returned result is = %FILTER_Hall%
RANGE: %FILTER_Hall% 1 0 // test if the hall sensor is activated
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#9.1: Test filter wheel driver and hall sensor feedback.
COMMAND: MLPRO2 CQ -800 // move it back to the hall sensor
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: MLPRO2 C1X // read the vaule to check if the hall sensor is activated 
READLINE: MLPRO2 FILTER_Hall 
Returned result is = %FILTER_Hall%
RANGE: %FILTER_Hall% 0 0 // test if the hall sensor is activated
SUB: TestPassOrFail



#10: Test Close up lens river and hall sensor feedback.
a. Connect the Motor Driver and Hall Sensor Jig (TE212) to the CONN5 and J1 on the UUT.
b. Click OK to continue.
IMPORTANT: Ensure that the Brown cable is fitted in the correct orientation.
DISPLAY: CloseUp.png
CLICK_OK:
COMMAND: MLPRO2 C3h// home it
DELAY: 1000
COMMAND: MLPRO2 C3z // stores 80 degrees in memory. (about 350 steps)
COMMAND: MLPRO2 C3=1				//1 = Move into optical path 
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: MLPRO2 C3X				// read the vaule to check if the hall sensor is activated 
READLINE: MLPRO2 CLOSEUP_Hall
Returned result is = %CLOSEUP_Hall%
// CLICK_OK:
RANGE: %CLOSEUP_Hall% 1 0
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#10.1:Test Close up lens river and hall sensor feedback.
COMMAND: MLPRO2 C3h// home it
DELAY: 2000
COMMAND: MLPRO2 C3X
READLINE: MLPRO2 CLOSEUP_Hall
Returned result is = %CLOSEUP_Hall%
// CLICK_OK:
RANGE: %CLOSEUP_Hall% 0 0
SUB: TestPassOrFail



#11: Test complete
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
IF: %FAILED% > 0
GOTO: #Failed:
ELSE: #Passed:


#Failed: a test failed
a. This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
b. Check the Log file for more details on the failed test(s).
IMPORTANT: This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
DISPLAY: test_failed.png
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #QUIT:

#Passed: next test
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish.
DISPLAY: AllTestsPassed.png
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: MLPRO2 C1Z
COMMAND: MLPRO2 C3Z
DISCONNECT: MLPRO2
DISCONNECT: TENMAPSU
// End of file
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
